is my idea good  i get asked this so many times from  different entrepreneurs who are trying  to launch a new company they're unsure  of themselves unsure of what they're  doing and they want  proof for me  that they should keep going they should  launch this thing  i'd like to flip the question on you  guys okay this is really important  because you can make money in any  industry any industry out there you can  make money in it if that's what you're  trying to do you can have success and  money in any industry  to make that happen  you have to bring yourself into it you  have to be super passionate about what  you're doing  and you have to bring a twist that other  people haven't done before  and that's going to be hard  that's going to force people to change  their habits there's going to be a lot  of resistance there's going to be a lot  of people who say no to you and you have  to be willing to suffer through all that  to eventually build your company  so for all of these ideas  they could be great  but do you have the passion behind it  and the fortitude  and conviction to stay with it  because if you do  it's fantastic if you don't the best  idea in the world will never go anywhere  i got a question from one of my readers  uh seth he's actually a youtube viewer  love you guys  seth is a student i want to open up his  own winery in michigan  and once eventually have his own winery  and sell the land underneath to sell the  condos and wanted my advice on it was a  good idea and what to do next  so why are you doing this seth what's  the reason for starting this business do  you love wine  are you passionate about wine do you  have a view of the way wineries should  be built that is different than what's  happening now  do you love helping people pick what  wine they should drink  and have opinions on  what wine goes with what food and and  why people are doing this all wrong if  you have that passion if you love wine  then go for it  this could be for you it's a great  opportunity you can make money in the  wine business  but if you're just trying to do it  because you think hey people spend a lot  of money on wine  i could sell this off in a couple years  do something else you probably won't  have a lot of success  so i'd examine your core reasons  if the reasons are good well-intentioned  want to make a difference want to help  people  then do it  and you'll have success  in terms of next steps seth said he was  uh trying to get a job at a winery to  learn the business and wanted my advice  on what to do  and that's the perfect way to do it you  know seth he's just graduating from  university looking for his first job  the best way to learn about the industry  is to go work in the industry  right for him to go and set up his own  winery right now would be  massively risky he doesn't know what  he's doing never had a business before  never been in the wine industry to set  up your own vineyard is going to cost  tons of money  and the chances of him being successful  will be tiny because he's never done it  before  but if you go work at a winery i would  pick a winery where you can connect with  the entrepreneur you believe in what  they're doing  they're willing to show you the ropes  you get involved as much as you can you  learn from them you learn not only the  job that you're hired for but you take  on extra projects every entrepreneur is  understaffed  so if you come in and you're a star  employee and you want to do more work  you want to help them with projects that  are outside your domain because you want  to learn  a good boss will give it to you so  that's the kind of person you want to go  work for i would be highly selective  of who you go work for and make sure  it's somebody who's going to give you  opportunities because you are taking  this job not to make money  it'll help keep you you know afloat but  that's not the main goal the goal is to  learn the goal is to get experience  supposed to get contacts the goal is to  make mistakes while getting paid this is  your real education this is your real  university  to give you the confidence contacts  experience so when you're ready to go  launch your own thing you know what to  do  i think you're on the right track  but again is it a good idea or not  only you can really answer that question  if you're in this for the right reasons  and it sounds like it that you are from  the passion you wrote in your in your  message  but that's going to be the real test  and for anybody else who's thinking the  same thing who's who's doubting  themselves and doubting their own ideas  and trying to get outsiders to give them  i guess encouragement and confidence  that hey somebody else believes in my  idea  the answer really lies within because  nobody can tell you if this is a good  business or not  it could be a great opportunity but if  you're not committed to it it's not  going to work and and you could take an  industry that's in the dumps where  nobody's making money on it and turn it  around into a great business  if you have the passion and conviction  fortitude to leg it out  believe  those you're watching like the video  please give it a thumbs up below and i  would love to hear what you have to  think leave a comment let me know what's  on your mind you have a question leave  it below i'll make a video response  thank you so much and i'll see you soon

